      "problem": "$\\frac{2}{9}÷3=$",
      "worked_solution": "Dividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number.\n\nThe reciprocal of $3$ is $\\frac{1}{3}.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{9}\\,÷\\,3=\\frac{2}{9}\\,\\times \\,\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{9}\\times \\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{2\\times 1}{9\\times 3}=\\frac{2}{27}\n$$",
